-- title:
--   Branch residues and orders at a supersingular crossing, swapped labelling
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p\ge 5$ and a package $\mathfrak X$ of type `DRModelPackage p`, a discrete valuation domain $O$ whose maximal ideal is generated by $p$, with fraction field $K$ and an embedding $\iota_K\colon K\to\overline{\mathbb Q}$; write $X_O$ for the base change `pullback (DRModel.toBase p) (Spec.map …)` of the two-chart integral model along $\operatorname{Spec} O\to\operatorname{Spec}\mathbb Z$, assumed integral, and let $x\in X_O$. Let $\varphi$ be a ring homomorphism from the function field of $X_O$ to $\overline{\mathbb Q}\otimes$-base change $\,$`modularFunctionFieldBar (1 * p)`, normalised by: on global sections coming from $a\in O$ it gives $\iota_K(a)$ (`hφO`), and on the finite $j$-chart algebra `chartAlgFin ℤ (modularFunctionFieldFull p) (IgusaScheme.jFull p)` it is the coefficientwise embedding `coeffEmb` of Laurent series (`hφj`), the relevant chart preimage being nonempty. Let $A\subset\overline{\mathbb Q}$ be a valuation subring, $k$ an algebraically closed perfect field of characteristic $p$, $\mathrm{red}\colon A\to k$, and let $P$ be a place specialisation at level $1$ and prime $p$ (for modular polynomial data satisfying the Kronecker congruence and integral Hecke $\bar\alpha,\bar\beta$) with prolongation tuple $R$; assume $\iota_K(O)\subseteq A$ and that $\mathrm{to}\kappa\colon O\to k$ is induced by $\mathrm{red}\circ\iota_K$. Let $w$ be a supersingular place of `modularFunctionFieldC k 1` (i.e. $w\in$ `ssPlaces p 1 k`), and assume $x$ is pinned to $w$: some $\hat\jmath\in O$ has $\mathrm{red}(\iota_K\hat\jmath)=w.\mathrm{evalAt}(\,$`jGeomGen k 1`$)$ and some $t$ in the maximal ideal of the local ring $\mathcal O_{X_O,x}$ satisfies $\varphi(t)=$`jFun 1 p`$-\iota_K(\hat\jmath)$. Let $n$ be a point of the fibre product of $\mathfrak X.\mathrm{compInf}\,k$ and $\mathfrak X.\mathrm{compZero}\,k$ whose two images $y_1=$`pullback.snd`$(n)$ and $y_2=$`pullback.fst`$(n)$ in $(\mathfrak X.\mathrm{ratModel}\,k).C$ are closed, such that $x$ is the image of $y_1$ under $\mathrm{compZero}\,k$ followed by `DRModel.baseChangeMap toκ` and the image of $y_2$ under $\mathrm{compInf}\,k$ followed by the same map, and such that the images of the generic point of $(\mathfrak X.\mathrm{ratModel}\,k).C$ under these two composites specialise to $x$. Assume further an element $t_F$ of $\mathcal O_{X_O,x}$ with $\varphi(t_F)=$`jQFun 1 p`$-($`jFun 1 p`$)^p$ whose image under the first specialisation map lies in the maximal ideal, and that $\varphi$ carries every germ at $x$ into the subring `R.nodeIntegers w` (elements integral for $R_1$, for $R_2$, and for every place $V$ of the level-$p$ field with $P.\mathrm{reduceFst}\,V=w$). The conclusion is that for every $s\in\mathcal O_{X_O,x}$: `R.nodeResidue₁ w` applied to $\varphi(s)$ vanishes if and only if $s$ lies in the pullback along the first specialisation map of the maximal ideal of the local ring at the generic point of the $\mathrm{compZero}$ branch; `R.nodeResidue₂ w` applied to $\varphi(s)$ vanishes if and only if $s$ lies in the corresponding prime for the $\mathrm{compInf}$ branch; the normalised order $\mathrm{ord}_w$ of the first residue equals the order at the place `placeOfPoint` of $y_1$ of the image of $s$ in the function field of $(\mathfrak X.\mathrm{ratModel}\,k).C$ under the stalk map of $\mathrm{compZero}$ followed by the base-change map, transported by `ffEquiv.symm`; and the order at the place $\mathrm{arithFrobC}\,p\,k\,1\cdot w$ of the second residue equals the corresponding order at `placeOfPoint` of $y_2$ along the $\mathrm{compInf}$ branch.
--
--   This is the dictionary, at a supersingular crossing of the Deligne–Rapoport model of $X_0(p)$ in characteristic $p$, between the two residue maps of a prolongation tuple read through the pinned embedding $\varphi$ and the two branch valuations of the characteristic-$p$ curve: kernels are matched with the branch primes of the local ring at the crossing, and orders with the local orders on the branches. The labelling used here assigns the first residue (taken at $w$) to the $\mathrm{compZero}$ branch and the second (taken at the arithmetic Frobenius translate of $w$) to the $\mathrm{compInf}$ branch, the mirror of the other convention, and it feeds the computation of node coordinates and of crossing widths.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_DRModelPackage_nodeResidue_eq_zero_iff_and_ord_eq_of_specializes_of_mem_maximalIdeal_swap.lean

